From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Subject: [PATCH] json_object: free a container object outside of assert()

json_object_put() frees a container object, after all of its children,
in a call inside assert(). A build with NDEBUG compiles that call out,
so every released object or array stays allocated.

Call the function before the assertion.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
--- a/json_object.c
+++ b/json_object.c
@@ -435,11 +435,14 @@ int json_object_put(struct json_object *
 		// All slots are cleared, now pop back up to the parent
 		{
 			json_object *parent = jso->_delete_parent;
+			int freed;
 			// jso is a child that's already been detached from its parent
 			// so we need to actually free it now
 			assert(jso->_ref_count == 0);
 			jso->_ref_count++;   // We're the exclusive owner of jso, non-atomic add is ok.
-			assert(_json_object_put_maybe_free(jso, 1) == 0);
+			freed = _json_object_put_maybe_free(jso, 1);
+			assert(freed == 0);
+			(void)freed;
 			jso = parent;
 			// iteration will be reset at the top of the loop
 		}
